import ../../../ui/source_language.dl

set source to the string form of "print line \"😀\""
set document to a UI source document named "main.dl" at "file:///workspace/main.dl" prefixed by "import lib/std.dl\n" containing source using UI CPU analysis
set other to a UI source document named "river.dl" at "file:///workspace/river.dl" prefixed by "import lib/river_challenge.dl\n\n" containing "get the hay in the boat" using UI CPU analysis
set client to a UI language client rooted at "file:///workspace"
set work to the next UI language work for client analyzing document at 0.0 seconds
require condition (work's step = 1) reporting "An editor did not prepare its project."
set files to the JSON member named "sources" in (work's payload)
require condition ((the JSON text named "main.dl" in files) = (document's prefix + source)) reporting "The source wrapper was not included in the analysis project."
free work's payload
set response to a new JSON-RPC null
set work to the UI language reply response at step 1 in client
free response
require condition (work's step = 2) reporting "The language service was not initialized."
free work's payload
set response to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON number "id" is 2, JSON child "result" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "capabilities" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "semanticTokensProvider" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "legend" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "tokenTypes" is (a JSON array containing [a new JSON-RPC text for "string"])])])])])]]
set work to the UI language reply response at step 2 in client
free response
free work's payload
set response to a new JSON-RPC array
set work to the UI language reply response at step 3 in client
free response
require condition (work's step = 4) reporting "The editor document was not opened."
set opened to the JSON member named "textDocument" in (the JSON member named "params" in (the JSON member named "message" in (work's payload)))
require condition ((the JSON text named "text" in opened) = (document's prefix + source)) reporting "Opening a document discarded its prefix."
free work's payload
set response to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON text "method" is "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", JSON child "params" is (a JSON object containing [JSON text "uri" is (document's uri), JSON child "diagnostics" is (a new JSON-RPC array)])]]
set work to the UI language reply response at step 4 in client
free response
require condition (work's step = 6) reporting "The editor did not request semantic tokens."
free work's payload
set response to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON number "id" is 6, JSON child "result" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "data" is (a new JSON-RPC array)])]]
set work to the UI language reply response at step 6 in client
free response
require condition ((work's step = 0) and (document's analyzed revision = document's revision)) reporting "The completed analysis did not belong to its document."
edit UI source document document to (the string form of "newer text") at 1.0 seconds
set work to the next UI language work for client analyzing document at 1.1 seconds
require condition (work's step = 0) reporting "The editor ignored its edit debounce."
set work to the next UI language work for client analyzing document at 1.3 seconds
require condition (work's step = 5) reporting "The changed source was not synchronized."
free work's payload
edit UI source document document to (the string form of "newest text") at 1.4 seconds
set revision to document's diagnostic revision
set response to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON text "method" is "textDocument/publishDiagnostics", JSON child "params" is (a JSON object containing [JSON text "uri" is (document's uri), JSON child "diagnostics" is (a new JSON-RPC array)])]]
set work to the UI language reply response at step 5 in client
free response
require condition (document's diagnostic revision = revision) reporting "Stale diagnostics replaced the document's current state."
free work's payload
set response to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON number "id" is 6, JSON child "result" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "data" is (a new JSON-RPC array)])]]
set work to the UI language reply response at step 6 in client
free response
require condition (document's analyzed revision != document's revision) reporting "Stale tokens marked newer source as analyzed."
set work to the next UI language work for client analyzing other at 2.0 seconds
require condition (work's step = 9) reporting "Switching editors did not close the preceding language document."
free work's payload
set response to a new JSON-RPC array
set work to the UI language reply response at step 9 in client
free response
require condition (work's step = 10) reporting "Switching editors did not prepare the new project."
set files to the JSON member named "sources" in (work's payload)
require condition ((files's length = 1) and ((the JSON text named "river.dl" in files) = (other's prefix + other's source))) reporting "One editor's files contaminated another editor's project."
free work's payload
set response to a new JSON-RPC null
set work to the UI language reply response at step 10 in client
free response
require condition ((work's step = 4) and (client's uri = other's uri)) reporting "The second editor retained the preceding URI."
free work's payload
set response to a new JSON-RPC array
set work to the UI language reply response at step 4 in client
free response
free work's payload
set response to a JSON array containing [a JSON object containing [JSON number "id" is 6, JSON child "result" is (a JSON object containing [JSON child "data" is (a new JSON-RPC array)])]]
set work to the UI language reply response at step 6 in client
free response
require condition (other's analyzed revision = other's revision) reporting "The River source did not use the shared analysis lifecycle."
free UI language client client
free UI source project (document's project)
free UI source project (other's project)
print line "Source editors share project lifecycle, prefixes, debouncing and stale-result isolation."
